# Cargo runs on a cheap subagent

Any `cargo` command is dispatched automatically. Do not run cargo in the parent shell, watch its log, or poll it. Do not wait for a special alias name.

Launch one background Haiku subagent (Claude Haiku 4.5) with the exact cargo command, then keep talking. Report only when its completion notice arrives.

| Command the parent was about to run | Subagent runs |
|---|---|
| `cargo check …` | that same command |
| `cargo build …` | that same command |
| `cargo build … --release` | that same command, with `CXXFLAGS="-include cstdint"` |
| `cargo test …` | that same command |
| `cargo fmt …` | that same command |
| `cargo clippy …` | that same command |

One cargo process at a time. A workspace-wide check, test, or build only when the user explicitly says workspace. Native target is `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`. Do not install binaries or restart services from a cargo run.
